Release: 24 September 2026 WP6 synthetic managed EV charging and fictional noncritical industrial demand-response pilots. Three illustrative EV departure-charge duties and three optional industrial jobs, identical useful work/charging per policy, unchanged nonshiftable safety/critical background, capacity/deadline/charging-efficiency constraints, arrival-order vs managed scheduling, 24-hour site load profiles and 9+9 sensitivity pairs. Separate whole-day/evening max site kW, site kWh and zero missed deadlines; modelled shift does NOT create energy savings. Two new interactive Pathways charts and individual duty/sensitivity tables; original cooling/TES pilot and previous historical research preserved. Neither pilot establishes measured Kerala EV behaviour, permission to flex KMML plant operations, grid-coincident Kerala MW, annual kWh/CO2, costs or calibrated 2040 scenarios.
